<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ t("progress.page.your-progress-targum", "Your Progress — targum") }}</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
{{ styles('tokens.css', 'shared.css', 'chrome.css', 'words.css', 'library.css', 'progress.css') }}
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{#- The level letter's 600, a real cut and never a faked bold (design.md §12, "Your level,
    v3", 2026-10-29). -#}
{{ hebrew_letters_face() }}
{{ script('keep.js') }}
{#- The key, before anything that reads it (targum-internal#343). `building.js`, and
    the conversation's pill, the followed series and the palette in the nav, each read `window.TARGUM_KEY`
    once as they load; it was set in a script at the foot of the body, so on a local serve
    they held an empty key for the life of the page and the bell, the followed series and
    the chat list were refused. The hosted box has no key and was never affected. -#}
<script>window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";</script>
</head>
{#- `words` as well as `progress`, for the same reason Learn carries it: the chart
    palette (--step-1..4) is defined on `.words`, and the tiles, the growth line and the
    stacked bar are all drawn with that kit. -#}
<body class="progress">
{#- The title stands on the desk under the bar, as on every desk page (design.md §12, "The
    boards are the desk", 2026-10-09). The nav draws it outside `main`, which stays hidden
    for a reader with nothing yet: the title is there either way. -#}
{% set here = 'progress' %}{% set title = t("you.page.your-progress", "Your Progress") %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
{{ script('building.js') }}

<main id="page" hidden>
  {#- A story in three parts under the totals (design.md §12, "Your Progress is a story in
      three parts", 2026-10-09): your level, how you got here, what next. -#}
  {#- The one block on this page that inverts. §9 allows a screen a single one and calls
      it the wake-up move — spent on one it is striking, spent on three it is a dark
      theme — so everything below here stays paper and ink. It is also the only surface
      the bright set is legal on: --leaf-bright does not reach 3:1 against paper. -#}
  <section class="ledger" id="ledger" aria-label="{{ t("progress.page.what-you-have-built", "Your totals") }}">
    <div class="counts" id="counts"></div>
    {#- What "learned on targum" counts, said under the totals wherever the figure is: it sat
        in part 2's time and words, which is hidden signed out, with recording stopped or
        with no record, while the figure always shows (qa on #858; targum-internal#471, B1).
        Inside the ledger as its quiet last line, not on the desk ground under it
        (targum-internal#522). -#}
    <p class="note ledger-note" id="learned-note">{{ t("progress.count.learned.note", "“Learned on targum” counts the words you marked here as anything other than known and have since marked known.") }}</p>
  </section>

  {#- Your level (design.md §12, "Your level, v3", 2026-10-29). The card's own heading,
      "Reading level", names the part (§12, "The level card says Reading level",
      2026-10-30). The card is the level and nothing else: the ulpan letter alone
      with its geresh, "About B2" beside it, a bar toward the next rung with the exact
      words to it, and the one press. The texts' own levels, A1 to Past C2, each row the
      texts at it you can read now or the words to go. And under the card, what you knew
      of what you read by Day, Week or Month. At a desk, two even columns: the card and
      the chart on the left, the ladder on the right. -#}
  <section class="story level" id="where" aria-labelledby="where-section">
    {#- Until the account answers, one quiet line, and on a failure Try again: an empty
        card said nothing, and What next said "None yet" to a reader with a record
        (targum-internal#471, B2). -#}
    <p class="quiet-line story-wait" id="where-wait" role="status">{{ t("progress.where.loading", "We're working out your level.") }}</p>
    <p class="quiet-line story-failed" id="where-failed" hidden>{{ t("progress.story.failed", "We couldn't load this part.") }}
      <button type="button" class="btn ghost outline story-again" id="story-again">{{ t("fault.try-again", "Try again") }}</button></p>
    <div class="level-grid" id="level-grid" hidden>
      <div class="card level-lead">
        {#- Visible, as the ladder's and the chart's heads are, and the one heading: the
            hidden h2 it replaces is gone (§12, "The level card says Reading level"). -#}
        <h2 class="level-title" id="where-section">{{ t("progress.level.title", "Reading level") }}</h2>
        {#- The letter leads, at the page title's step, in ink; its name is said before
            it and the glyph itself is hidden from a screen reader (design P0-6). The bar
            is not spoken (§12, "See all keeps one level, and the bar is not spoken"):
            the words line under it is, once, as text. -#}
        <p class="level-mark" id="level-mark" hidden><span class="visually-hidden" id="level-spoken"></span><bdi class="level-big" id="level-big"></bdi><span class="level-cefr" id="level-cefr"></span></p>
        <p class="level-head" id="where-title"></p>
        <p class="level-step" id="where-step" hidden></p>
        <p class="level-known" id="where-known" hidden></p>
        <div class="level-toward" id="level-toward" hidden>
          <div class="level-bar" id="level-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="level-fill" id="level-fill"></span></div>
          <p class="level-togo" id="level-togo"></p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn filled level-go" id="where-go" href="/library" hidden></a>
        <p class="note level-note" id="where-note" hidden></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card level-ladder" id="ladder" hidden>
        <p class="level-ladder-head" id="ladder-head">{{ t("progress.ladder.head", "Texts by level") }}</p>
        <ol class="touchstones" id="touchstones" aria-labelledby="ladder-head"></ol>
      </div>
      {#- What the reader knew of what they read (targum-internal#291): the share of the
          running words in each finished section that were marked known on the day it was
          finished, kept then and never recomputed, by Day, Week or Month (design.md §12,
          "Your level, v3"). The one figure here allowed to fall. Read from the account, so
          absent signed out, and absent until two days have points. Drawn by
          `progress.js`. -#}
      <div class="card reading" id="reading" hidden>
        <div class="reading-head">
          <h3 class="reading-title" id="reading-title">{{ t("progress.reading.title", "Words you knew") }}</h3>
          <div class="seg reading-by" id="reading-by" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("progress.reading.by", "Show by") }}">
            <button type="button" data-by="day" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("progress.reading.by-day", "Day") }}</button>
            <button type="button" data-by="week" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("progress.reading.by-week", "Week") }}</button>
            <button type="button" data-by="month" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("progress.reading.by-month", "Month") }}</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="reading-line"></div>
        <p class="visually-hidden" id="reading-live" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="reading-words" id="reading-said"></div>
        <p class="quiet-line reading-failed" id="reading-failed" hidden>{{ t("progress.story.failed", "We couldn't load this part.") }}
          <button type="button" class="btn ghost outline story-again" id="reading-again">{{ t("fault.try-again", "Try again") }}</button></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- 2 · How you got here (design.md §12, "How you got here: two figures, the days active
      and the words of the period", 2026-10-30): the period at the head's end; words read
      and time listening, read off the account's record of what happened in each text
      (#127), each against the period before; the days active; and the period's words. -#}
  <section class="panel story" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="how-head">
      <div class="how-titles">
        <p class="story-step">{{ t("progress.story.how", "How you got here") }}</p>
        <h2 id="how-title" class="section-title story-head"></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="seg how-by" id="how-by" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("progress.reading.by", "Show by") }}" hidden>
        <button type="button" data-period="7" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("progress.reading.by-week", "Week") }}</button>
        <button type="button" data-period="30" aria-pressed="true">{{ t("progress.reading.by-month", "Month") }}</button>
        <button type="button" data-period="" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("progress.spent.ever", "All time") }}</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="spent" id="spent" hidden>
      <div class="spent-figures" id="spent-figures"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" id="spent-off" hidden>{{ t("progress.spent.off", "We're not showing time and words because recording is stopped. You can start it again in Your account.") }}</p>
    <div class="how-lower" id="how-lower" hidden>
      <div class="how-days" id="how-days" hidden>
        <h3 class="how-sub" id="days-title"></h3>
        <div class="days" id="days-grid" role="img"></div>
        <p class="days-range" id="days-range" aria-hidden="true"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-words" id="how-words" hidden>
        <h3 class="how-sub" id="words-title"></h3>
        <div class="how-bars" id="words-bars"></div>
        <p class="how-since" id="words-since" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- 3 · What next: the words still being learned that keep coming round, and texts at
      the reader's level now. -#}
  <section class="panel story" id="next" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <p class="story-step">{{ t("progress.story.next", "What next") }}</p>
    <h2 id="next-title" class="section-title story-head">{{ t("progress.next.title", "The words and texts that would help most") }}</h2>
    <div class="next-halves">
      <div class="next-half" id="next-words">
        <h3 class="story-sub" id="next-words-title">{{ t("progress.next.words", "Words you keep meeting and don't know yet") }}</h3>
        <ul class="next-rows" id="met-rows"></ul>
        <p class="quiet-line" id="met-empty" hidden></p>
        <a class="next-more" id="practise" href="/words">{{ t("progress.next.practise", "Practise these words") }} →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="next-half" id="next-texts">
        <h3 class="story-sub" id="next-texts-title">{{ t("progress.next.texts", "Texts at your level now") }}</h3>
        <ul class="next-rows" id="level-rows"></ul>
        <p class="note" id="level-empty" hidden></p>
        <a class="next-more" id="more-texts" href="/library">{{ t("progress.next.library", "More in the Library") }} →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

{#- Before the foot, not after it: it was drawn under the foot, so a reader with
    nothing yet saw the site's foot and then the page's one line (2026-09-28). -#}
{#- A line and a press, in a card on the desk (polish 8, targum-internal#471): it was one
    line of text on the desk ground with a link inside it. -#}
<section class="panel nothing" id="nothing" hidden>
  <p>{{ t("progress.page.nothing-yet", "Your progress starts with the first word you mark in a text.") }}</p>
  <p><a class="btn filled" id="library-link" href="/library">{{ t("progress.page.open-the-library", "Open the Library") }}</a></p>
</section>
{#- Where the account never answered (errors QA, targum-internal#468): a refusal, a dropped
    connection or no connection at all said "Your progress starts with the first word you
    mark" to a reader with a record, which reads as everything gone. The panel is the one
    home and Your Words draw. -#}
<section class="fault-panel page-fault" id="progress-fault" role="alert" hidden>
  <p class="fault-panel-said" id="progress-fault-lede">{{ t("progress.page.failed", "We couldn't load your progress.") }}</p>
  <div class="fault-panel-row">
    <button type="button" class="fault-go" id="progress-fault-again">{{ t("fault.try-again", "Try again") }}</button>
    <span class="fault-fact" id="progress-fault-says">{{ t("progress.page.failed-says", "Everything you've marked is still here.") }}</span>
    <button type="button" class="fault-act" id="progress-fault-tell" data-tell-us>{{ t("fault.tell-us", "Tell us") }}</button>
  </div>
</section>
{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}


<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
{% if strings %}window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};
{% endif %}</script>
{{ script('strings.js') }}
{{ script('charts.js') }}
{{ script('lang.js') }}
{{ script('vocab.js') }}
{{ script('sync.js') }}
{{ script('account.js') }}
{{ script('progress.js') }}
</body>
</html>
